window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["su-04.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">شرح الدليل الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> ابحث عن الرمز أو الجزء بنفس اسمه الإنكليزي.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">B = كهرباء الجسم: 4</span><span class=\"en-chip\">C = الهيكل والحساسات: 13</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 9</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">26 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2199-16 battery voltage - circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2199-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With Ignition On. Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses voltage input below 8.0 volts for 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM Indicator lamp illuminated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>LOW VOLTAGE POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</li><li>FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery is fully charged before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any battery or charging systems DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>(A943) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the TPM Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check (A943) Fused B(+) circuit in the TPM Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A943) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>(Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit in the TPM Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (Z922) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>INTERMITTENT WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Wiggle test the wiring harness and connectors while monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for the data to change or for the DTC to reset during the wiggle test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>While monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Look for the data to change other than as expected or for the DTC to reset.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2199-17 battery voltage - circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2199-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses voltage input above 16.0 volts for 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System operates normally</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>HIGH VOLTAGE POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any PCM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INTERMITTENT WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Wiggle test the wiring harness and connectors while monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for the data to change or for the DTC to reset during the wiggle test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>While monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Look for the data to change other than as expected or for the DTC to reset.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b21dd-84 system voltage - signal below allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B21DD-84</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL BELOW ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أقل من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With Ignition On. Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses voltage input below 8.0 volts for 20 ms seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM Indicator lamp illuminated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</li><li>FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any battery or charging system DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>(A943) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the TPM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check (A943) Fused B(+) circuit in the Tire Pressure Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A943) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>(Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit in the Tire Pressure Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (Z922) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>INTERMITTENT WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Wiggle test the wiring harness and connectors while monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for the data to change or for the DTC to reset during the wiggle test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>While monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Look for the data to change other than as expected or for the DTC to reset.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b21dd-85 system voltage - signal above allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B21DD-85</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL ABOVE ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أعلى من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module is receiving CAN messages that system voltage is above 16.0 volts for 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPMS system operates as normal</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT SHORT TO VOLTAGE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Tun the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any battery or charging system DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INTERMITTENT WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Wiggle test the wiring harness and connectors while monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for the data to change or for the DTC to reset during the wiggle test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>While monitoring the scan tool data relative to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Look for the data to change other than as expected or for the DTC to reset.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c0077-00 low tire pressure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C0077-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOW TIRE PRESSURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With Ignition On. Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses low pressure condition when the tire pressure falls below or is equal to the low pressure threshold value as specified for the vehicle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM Indicator lamp illuminated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TIRE PRESSURE</li><li>INCORRECT PLACARD VALUES</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            DO NOT REPLACE TPM SENSOR. THIS FAULT IS EXPECTED IF TIRE PRESSURE IS 20% BELOW THE PLACARD PRESSURE</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Inflate tire to cold placard pressure to remove the fault condition</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            It is recommended to inflate tire 2 psi past placard pressure to ensure fault condition clears.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 5 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update. Test Complete</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION. .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1501-96 tire pressure sensor 1 - internal component failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1501-96</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR 1 - INTERNAL COMPONENT FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor actively monitors the air pressure, air temperature inside the tire, the direction of the tire rotation and the internal battery status. Each sensor has a unique ID code. The TPM Sensor transmits the data at regular intervals via an encoded signal to a receiver circuit located in the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts. Vehicle speed above 24 km/h (15 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives RF signal error if data is not received or cannot be accurately decoded for a maximum of 20 minutes when the vehicle speed is above 24 km/h (15 mph). Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives internal sensor hardware error. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses error in the shock sensor, pressure sensor, or temperature sensor.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module Lamp will flash on and off for 75 seconds then remain on solid. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>AFTERMARKET TIRES/WHEELS</li><li>INTERMITTENT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL DTC</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li><li>NOTE:           In the Scan Tool under Data &quot;FF&quot; is the default value. If this value is displayed,</li><li>the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module has not been programmed.</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This fault can be set if the spare tire is currently installed on the vehicle, and it is not equipped with a TPM Sensor.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) up to 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module and locate the following:</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Tire 1 Pressure Sensor HW Defective Tire 1 Rotation Detection HW Defective Tire 1 Loss of Sensor Signal Tire 1 Missing Sensor ID Tire 1 Duplicate Sensor ID</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do any of the above faults read &quot;Set&quot;?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR CORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform a visual inspection to verify that all road wheels are equipped with a TPM Sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) verify the correct TPM Sensor is on the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer Tool to scan each TPM Sensor for a response. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly for that Model Year and Vehicle Line Code and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel. If no response replace the sensor</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the correct TPM Sensor installed on the vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT SET USING TPM-RKE ANALYZER</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The following procedure is used to locate the TPM Sensor that is setting the internal fault. If the tires have been rotated, the TPM Sensor is no longer in sequence from the factory. Faults are linked to the TPM Sensor IDs. You MUST locate the TPM Sensor that set the fault before continuing. Use the following method below at every tire location.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the TPM Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the TPM Sensor will not respond to the tool.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for a response, and store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the TPM Sensor if the results show a &quot;Damaged Accel&quot;, &quot;Damaged Temp&quot;, &quot;Damaged Press&quot;, &quot;H/W fail&quot;, &quot;S/W fail&quot; or the TPM Sensor does not respond after repeated attempts. Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL . Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check to see if the Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Has the TPM Sensor been located?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT - MISMATCHED ID</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to verify the TPM Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module. The TPM Sensor Identifications are located under &quot;Data Display&quot; for the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Do the TPM Sensor IDs match what is stored in the TPM Module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1502-96 tire pressure sensor 2 - internal component failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1502-96</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR 2 - INTERNAL COMPONENT FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor actively monitors the air pressure, air temperature inside the tire, the direction of the tire rotation and the internal battery status. Each sensor has a unique ID code. The TPM Sensor transmits the data at regular intervals via an encoded signal to a receiver circuit located in the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts. Vehicle speed above 24 km/h (15 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives RF signal error if data is not received or cannot be accurately decoded for a maximum of 20 minutes when the vehicle speed is above 24 km/h (15 mph). Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives internal sensor hardware error. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses error in the shock sensor, pressure sensor, or temperature sensor.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module Lamp will flash on and off for 75 seconds then remain on solid. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>AFTERMARKET TIRES/WHEELS</li><li>INTERMITTENT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL DTC</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This fault can be set if the spare tire is currently installed on the vehicle, and it is not equipped with a TPM Sensor.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) up to 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module and locate the following: Tire 2 Pressure Sensor HW Defective Tire 2 Rotation Detection HW Defective Tire 2 Loss of Sensor Signal Tire 2 Missing Sensor ID Tire 2 Duplicate Sensor ID</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do any of the above faults read &quot;Set&quot;?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR CORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform a visual inspection to verify that all road wheels are equipped with a TPM Sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) verify the correct TPM Sensor is on the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer Tool to scan each TPM Sensor for a response. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly for that Model Year and Vehicle Line Code and repeat the process on</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">each non-responsive wheel. If no response replace the sensor</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the correct TPM Sensor installed on the vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT SET USING TPM - RKE ANALYZER</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The following procedure is used to locate the TPM Sensor that is setting the internal fault. If the tires have been rotated, the TPM Sensor is no longer in sequence from the factory. Faults are linked to the TPM Sensor IDs. You MUST locate the TPM Sensor that set the fault before continuing. Use the following method below at every tire location.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the TPM Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the TPM Sensor will not respond to the tool.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for a response, and store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the TPM Sensor if the results show a &quot;Damaged Accel&quot;, &quot;Damaged Temp&quot;, &quot;Damaged Press&quot;, &quot;H/W fail&quot;, &quot;S/W fail&quot; or the TPM Sensor does not respond after repeated attempts. Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL . Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check to see if the Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Has the TPM Sensor been located?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT - MISMATCHED ID</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to verify the TPM Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module. The TPM Sensor Identifications are located under &quot;Data Display&quot; for the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Do the TPM Sensor IDs match what is stored in the TPM Module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1503-96 tire pressure sensor 3 - internal component failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1503-96</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR 3 - INTERNAL COMPONENT FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor actively monitors the air pressure, air temperature inside the tire, the direction of the tire rotation and the internal battery status. Each sensor has a unique ID code. The TPM Sensor transmits the data at regular intervals via an encoded signal to a receiver circuit located in the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts. Vehicle speed above 24 km/h (15 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives RF signal error if data is not received or cannot be accurately decoded for a maximum of 20 minutes when the vehicle speed is above 24 km/h (15 mph). Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives internal sensor hardware error. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses error in the shock sensor, pressure sensor, or temperature sensor.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module Lamp will flash on and off for 75 seconds then remain on solid. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>AFTERMARKET TIRES/WHEELS</li><li>INTERMITTENT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL DTC</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This fault can be set if the spare tire is currently installed on the vehicle, and it is not equipped with a TPM Sensor.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) up to 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module and locate the following: Tire 3 Pressure Sensor HW Defective Tire 3 Rotation Detection HW Defective Tire 3 Loss of Sensor Signal Tire 3 Missing Sensor ID Tire 3 Duplicate Sensor ID</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do any of the above faults read &quot;Set&quot;?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR CORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform a visual inspection to verify that all road wheels are equipped with a TPM Sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) verify the correct TPM Sensor is on the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer Tool to scan each TPM Sensor for a response. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly for that Model Year and Vehicle Line Code and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel. If no response replace the sensor</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the correct TPM Sensor installed on the vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT SET USING TPM-RKE ANALYZER</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The following procedure is used to locate the TPM Sensor that is setting the internal fault. If the tires have been rotated, the TPM Sensor is no longer in sequence from the factory. Faults are linked to the TPM Sensor IDs. You MUST locate the TPM Sensor that set the fault before continuing. Use the following method below at every tire location.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the TPM Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the TPM Sensor will not respond to the tool.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for a response, and store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the TPM Sensor if the results show a &quot;Damaged Accel&quot;, &quot;Damaged Temp&quot;, &quot;Damaged Press&quot;, &quot;H/W fail&quot;, &quot;S/W fail&quot; or the TPM Sensor does not respond after repeated attempts. Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL . Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check to see if the Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Has the TPM Sensor been located?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT - MISMATCHED ID</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to verify the TPM Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module. The TPM Sensor Identifications are located under &quot;Data Display&quot; for the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Do the TPM Sensor IDs match what is stored in the TPM Module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1504-96 tire pressure sensor 4 - internal component failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1504-96</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR 4 - INTERNAL COMPONENT FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor actively monitors the air pressure, air temperature inside the tire, the direction of the tire rotation and the internal battery status. Each sensor has a unique ID code. The TPM Sensor transmits the data at regular intervals via an encoded signal to a receiver circuit located in the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts. Vehicle speed above 24 km/h (15 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives RF signal error if data is not received or cannot be accurately decoded for a maximum of 20 minutes when the vehicle speed is above 24 km/h (15 mph). Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives internal sensor hardware error. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module senses error in the shock sensor, pressure sensor, or temperature sensor.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module Lamp will flash on and off for 75 seconds then remain on solid. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>AFTERMARKET TIRES/WHEELS</li><li>INTERMITTENT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL DTC</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This fault can be set if the spare tire is currently installed on the vehicle, and it is not equipped with a TPM Sensor.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) up to 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module and locate the following: Tire 4 Pressure Sensor HW Defective Tire 4 Rotation Detection HW Defective Tire 4 Loss of Sensor Signal Tire 4 Missing Sensor ID Tire 4 Duplicate Sensor ID</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do any of the above faults read &quot;Set&quot;?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR CORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR 1.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform a visual inspection to verify that all road wheels are equipped with a TPM Sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) verify the correct TPM Sensor is on the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer Tool to scan each TPM Sensor for a response. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly for that Model Year and Vehicle Line Code and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel. If no response replace the sensor</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the correct TPM Sensor installed on the vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT SET USING TPM-RKE ANALYZER</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The following procedure is used to locate the TPM Sensor that is setting the internal fault. If the tires have been rotated, the TPM Sensor is no longer in sequence from the factory. Faults are linked to the TPM Sensor IDs. You MUST locate the TPM Sensor that set the fault before continuing. Use the following method below at every tire location.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the TPM Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the TPM Sensor will not respond to the tool.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for a response, and store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the TPM Sensor if the results show a &quot;Damaged Accel&quot;, &quot;Damaged Temp&quot;, &quot;Damaged Press&quot;, &quot;H/W fail&quot;, &quot;S/W fail&quot; or the TPM Sensor does not respond after repeated attempts. Install the correct Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL . Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check to see if the Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Has the TPM Sensor been located?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT - MISMATCHED ID</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to verify the TPM Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module. The TPM Sensor Identifications are located under &quot;Data Display&quot; for the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Do the TPM Sensor IDs match what is stored in the TPM Module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c151c-00 tire pressure sensors missing\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C151C-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE SENSORS MISSING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When installing a new Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module, the module is programed with universal IDs for the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensors. The TPM Module must be programmed with the correct TPM Sensor ID&#x27;s.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts. Vehicle TPM Sensor ID locate process</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">New Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module installed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM ECU will not be able to monitor all wheel positions until autolearn detects a correct TPM Sensor ID set. TPM Indicator lamp illuminated. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>INCORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR ID(S)</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li><li>NOTE:           In the Scan Tool under Data &quot;FF&quot; is the default value. If this value is displayed,</li><li>the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module has not been programmed.</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>VERIFY DTC IS ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 20 minutes in order to receive TPM data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR ID(S)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the Sensor will not respond to the tool.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If you receive no response from any of the tire pressure sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly, and repeat the process on each of the non-responsive wheel(s)</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for an ID, store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer to upload the correct IDs and proper locations in the scan tool.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, select the TPM Module under &quot;Miscellaneous Functions&quot;, follow the procedure for uploading TPM Sensor IDs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, erase TPM Module DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 20 minutes in order to receive TPM data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, check to see if the TPM sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do the TPM IDs match?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c151d-00 tire pressure sensor location undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C151D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR LOCATION UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The vehicle Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor locate process occurs after the vehicle is stationary for more than 20 min. The TPM system will determine the sensor positions while driving at speeds above 24 km/h (15 mph). This process can take up to 20 min to determine TPM Sensor positions.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts. Vehicle TPM Sensor locate process.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">New Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module has never attempted localization. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module fails multiple vehicle TPM Sensor locate processes. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module fails Left/Right or Front/Rear Sensor locate processes. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensors are present on first drive, the TPM Sensor location cannot be determined/guaranteed (cannot revert to last known good locations).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">VERIFY DTC IS ACTIVE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The DTC C151D should not exist on its own. If any other DTCs are present, refer to the DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX first before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If a new TPM Module was installed, the vehicle must remain stationary for 20 minutes before proceeding with this diagnostic procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, erase TPM Module DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is DTC C151D active on its own at this time?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1570-00 duplicate tire pressure sensor ids\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1570-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DUPLICATE TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR IDS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When installing a new Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module, the module is programed with universal IDs for the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensors. The TPM Module must be programmed with the correct TPM Sensor IDs or drive the vehicle for a minimum of 20 minutes with vehicle speed greater than 32 km/h (20 mph).</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>SENSOR IDS NOT DOWNLOADED INTO TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>INCORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR IDS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li><li>NOTE:             In the Scan Tool under Data &quot;FF&quot; is the default value. If this value is displayed,</li><li>the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module has not been programmed.</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ACTIVE DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/r (15 mph) for 20 minutes in order to receive TPM data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Intermittent DTC Procedure. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR IDS AFTER UPLOADING THEM WITH TPM-RKE TOOL</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the Sensor will not respond to the tool.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If you receive no response from any of the tire pressure sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly, and repeat the process on each of the non-responsive wheel(s)</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for an ID, store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer to upload the correct IDs and proper locations in the scan tool.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, select the TPM Module under &quot;Miscellaneous Functions&quot;, follow the procedure for uploading TPM Sensor IDs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, erase TPM Module DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/r (15 mph) for 20 minutes in order to receive TPM data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, check to see if the TPM sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do the TPM IDs match?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs. If any displayed, perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. If there are none, repeat this test. A bad TPM will have other DTCs set.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1580-00 left/right side tire pressure sensor location undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1580-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT/RIGHT SIDE TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR LOCATION UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components before beginning this diagnostic procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             The vehicle must remain stationary for 20 minutes before proceeding with this diagnostic procedure.</div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The vehicle Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor locate process occurs after the vehicle remains stationary for 20 minutes. The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module will determine the TPM Sensor positions. The TPM Sensors themselves determine which side of the vehicle they are located on.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts. Vehicle TPM Sensor locate process.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">New Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module has never attempted localization. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module fails multiple vehicle TPM sensor locate processes if localization fails due to Left/Right sensor failure.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM system operates as normal</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR INTERNAL FAULT ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module and locate the following for each TPM</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Sensor: Tire Pressure Sensor HW Fault Tire Temperature Sensor HW Fault Tire Acceleration Sensor HW Fault</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do any of the above HW faults read &quot;Set&quot;?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">For each TPM Sensor with a HW Fault. Install a new Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1581-00 front/rear tire pressure sensor location undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1581-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FRONT/REAR TIRE PRESSURE SENSOR LOCATION UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components before beginning this diagnostic procedure.</div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The vehicle Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor locate process occurs after the vehicle remains stationary for 20 minutes. The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module will determine the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor positions. The TPM Module measures the signal strength of each TPM sensor and determines if the are in the front or rear.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 8.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">New Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module has never attempted localization. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module fails multiple vehicle TPM sensor locate processes if localization fails due to Front/Rear sensor failure.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE HARNESS</li><li>INCORRECT TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE INSTALLATION</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The vehicle must remain stationary for 20 minutes before proceeding with this diagnostic procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify that all tire pressures are to the recommended cold inflation tire pressure specifications.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 10 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE INTERFERENCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Interference may occur if the TPM Module is installed incorrectly or the TPM harness is not fastened properly to the body.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify the following: Aftermarket devices are installed or in the vehicle. The TPM Module harness is damaged or is routed incorrectly. The TPM Module is installed incorrectly.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there any of the above conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1597-00 tpm system deactivated - winter mode\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1597-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TPM SYSTEM DEACTIVATED - WINTER MODE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components before beginning this diagnostic procedure.</div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            When this DTC is active the TPM Module will enter a deactivation mode (Winter Mode) and the TPM system becomes deactivated. If winter tires and wheel assemblies are installed no repair is required.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Tire Pressure Monitor (TPM) Module determines the TPM Sensor positions by performing the vehicle Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor locate procedure. This procedure is run after the vehicle has been stationary for 20 minutes. After driving the vehicle at speeds greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for a minimum of 10 minutes without the TPM Sensor installed, the TPM Module sends a bus message commanding the TPM telltale lamp to flash for 75 seconds. After the 75 seconds of flashing, the lamp will remain on solid and a chime will be heard. The message center will display SERVICE TPM SYSTEM for five seconds and shut off, all while the tire pressure values will be displayed as dashes. After the ignition has been cycled off and on the TPM telltail lamp will remain off, the message center will no longer display SERVICE TPM SYSTEM, and the tire pressures continue to be displayed as dashes.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts. Vehicle TPM Sensor locate process.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">BUX/Canada vehicles only. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module where all four TPM Sensors fail the locate processes at the same time. TPM Sensors not installed on winter tire and wheel assemblies.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System is operating normally. TPM Indicator lamp illuminated. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSORS NOT PRESENT</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSORS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Repair all other TPM Module DTCs before continuing with this test procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Drive the vehicle at speeds greater than 24 km/h (15 mph) for 10 minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC PROCEDURE. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) WINTER MODE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for the following conditions: The telltale lamp is off. The tire pressure values in the Instrument Cluster are displayed as dashes. The message center is not displaying &quot;SERVICE TPM SYSTEM&quot;.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are all of the above conditions correct?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module is now in deactivation mode (Winter Mode). This DTC will remain active until the correct tire and wheel assemblies are installed back on the vehicle. Once one of the correct tire and wheel assemblies are reinstalled, the other three must also be reinstalled prior to turning the ignition on.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Verify the correct TPM Sensors are installed in all of the tire and wheel assemblies.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the correct TPM Sensors installed?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Install all new Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensors in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c15d6-00 run flat tire pressure below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C15D6-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RUN FLAT TIRE PRESSURE BELOW THRESHOLD</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With Ignition On. Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts. Engine run time above 3 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module receives a valid RF Message from a TPM sensor equipped to a road tire (i.e. not the spare) where the pressure value is approximately 14.5 PSI below the placard pressure of the axle to which the sensor has been located. Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor location has failed to the higher of the 2 axle placard pressures.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM Indicator lamp illuminated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DAMAGED/LEAKING TIRE</li><li>LOW TIRE PRESSURE</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) SENSOR LOCATION</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Before beginning diagnostic procedure, verify that all the tire pressures are correct and compared to the placard pressure settings.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          When checking all tire pressures, verify any tire leaks or damage have been repaired/replaced as needed.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at a speed greater than 32 km/h (20 mph) up to 20 minutes in order to receive TPM Sensor data and allow for the system to update.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test Complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TPM-RKE ANALYZER</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The following procedure is used to locate the TPM Sensor that is setting the internal fault. If the tires have been rotated, the TPM Sensor is no longer in sequence from the factory. Faults are linked to the TPM Sensor IDs. You MUST locate the TPM Sensor that set the fault before continuing. Use the following method below at every tire location.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the TPM Sensor IDs do not match, it may be necessary to move the vehicle to a location away from other TPM Sensors and repeat this step.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Always be certain to select the proper vehicle line and model year when using this tool, as the tool will automatically use the correct protocol to attempt to read the TPM Sensor. If the incorrect vehicle line and/or model year is selected, the TPM Sensor will not respond to the tool.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use a TPM-RKE Analyzer (special tool #2046300080, Kit, TPM/RKE ANALYZER) to scan each TPM Sensor for a response, and store in the proper location in the TPM-RKE Analyzer. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, select Data Display for the TPM Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check to see if the Sensor IDs match what is programmed into the TPM Module.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Some vehicles will not receive the TPM Sensor data when the vehicle is stationary. The vehicle may need to be driven at speeds greater than 32 km/h (20 mph) for about a minute in order to receive TPM Sensor data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Has the TPM Sensor been located?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Install the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. If you receive no response from any of the TPM Sensors, check to make sure that the TPM-RKE Analyzer is set correctly and repeat the process on each non-responsive wheel.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2209-00 tire pressure monitor internal\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2209-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TIRE PRESSURE MONITOR INTERNAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components before beginning this diagnostic procedure.</div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuously Battery voltage between 9 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module detects an internal fault</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM ECU will attempt to enter shutdown mode. TPM Indicator lamp illuminated. For Premium systems &quot;Service TPM System&quot; message displayed and pressure values replaced by dashes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NON-FCC COMPLIANT COMPONENTS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE - INTERNAL FAULT</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for and remove any non-FCC compliant components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0001-00 can c bus\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0001-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. Engine run time above 3 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module does not receive any Can C bus messages for a specific amount of time. One trip fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System is operating normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN C BUS OPEN OR SHORTED CONDITION</li><li>DTCS RELATED TO BATTERY VOLTAGE, IGNITION, OR VIN MESSAGES</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) POWER AND GROUND</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>MODULE THAT SET THIS DTC</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE COMMUNICATION DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          For vehicle communication problems, use the scan tool to refer to the Network Review Screen. The screen depicts a high level view of the vehicle network. Fault and problem areas appear in red. Selecting any of the network components allows access to the source of the problem.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, select View DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the U0001-Can C Bus circuit diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Stored Lost Communication DTCs diagnostic procedure. Refer to STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0100-00 lost communication with ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0100-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ECM/PCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0121-00 lost communication with anti-lock brake system (abs) control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0121-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MODULE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0155-00 lost communication with cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0155-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0401-00 implausible data received from ecm-pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0401-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ECM-PCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ECM-PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System is operating normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK IF PCM DTCS ARE PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any PCM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM Verification Test. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0415-00 implausible data received from abs\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0415-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ABS</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ABS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System is operating normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE DTCS</li><li>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE DTCS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR DTCS IN THE ABS MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the ABS Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the ABS Module reporting any DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM Verification Test. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0422-00 implausible data received from body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0422-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Body Control Module (BCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System is operating normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CAN BUS DTCS ARE PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any BCM CAN BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedures. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Body Control Module (BCM) pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TPM Verification Test. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0423-00 implausible data received from cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0423-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Body Control Module (BCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TPM System is operating normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>INSTRUMENT PANEL CLUSTER (IPC) DTCS</li><li>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</li><li>INSTRUMENT PANEL CLUSTER (IPC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Was the TPM Module replaced during the test procedure?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TPM MODULE REPLACEMENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the previously removed and/or disconnected components and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, go to &quot;Tire Pressure Module (TPM)&quot;, select &quot;Miscellaneous Functions&quot; and perform the Proxy Alignment procedure.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, go into the Body Control Module (BCM) or (TIPMCGW), Select &quot;Misc Functions&quot; then &quot;Updated Pressure Thresholds&quot; and read &quot;&#x27;Front Tire Placard Press (Hvy Ld)&quot; and &quot;&#x27;Rear Tire Placard Press (Hvy Ld)&quot; to confirm the values were programmed correctly. If the Placard values are incorrect in the BCM or TIPMCGW Module, select &quot;Continue&quot; and enter the placard pressure value as seen on the Tire Inflation Pressure (Placard) label and save it to the Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all stored DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are there any DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair not complete, perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>TPM SENSOR REPLACEMENT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If a TPM-RKE Tool is not available, let the vehicle sit stationary for more then 20 minutes, and then proceed to step #4 below.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using an updated TPM-RKE Analyzer Tool, select TPM Functions, then enter the Model Year and the Body Style of the vehicle, and for the Trigger Selection select PARK SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Scan each TPM Sensor at each road wheel, and store each TPM Sensor ID in the correct location. (LEFT FRONT, LEFT REAR, RIGHT FRONT, RIGHT REAR, and SPARE TIRE (if equipped).)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Scan Tool, Go to &quot;TPM&quot;, then &quot;Misc Function&quot; and choose the corresponding wheel to Program the Sensor ID. (ID can be obtained on Sensor itself or can be read via the TPM-RKE Analyzer tool)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Drive the vehicle for a minimum of 20 minutes while maintaining a continuous speed above 24 km/h (15 mph).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TPM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are there any TPM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910359</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
